1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,020
我是杰森.西弗，是个心理医生
Hi, I'm Jason Seaver. I'm a psychiatrist.

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:07,120
过去15年里 我致力于解决患者的问题
I've spent the last 15 years helping people with their problems.

3
00:00:07,165 --> 00:00:08,534
我是麦姬.西弗
And I'm Maggie Seaver.

4
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,620
过去15年里，我一直围着孩子们转
I've spent the last 15 years helping our kids with problems...

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,000
解决那些杰森也束手无策的问题
even Jason wouldn't believe.

6
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:16,800
现在麦姬已重操旧业 在一家当地报社做记者
Now, Maggie has gone back to work as a reporter for the local newspaper.

7
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:20,400
杰森把他的诊所搬到了家里 这样就可以陪着孩子们了
Jason has moved his practice into the house so he can be there for the kids.

8
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,580
-他们是可爱的孩子 -大多时候都是
- They're great kids. - Most of the time.

9
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:25,683
-但是有时… -反正我们很爱他们
- And the rest of the time? - We love them anyway.

10
00:00:25,683 --> 00:00:27,051
是的
Yeah.

11
00:00:27,218 --> 00:00:28,927
鬼才相信
Unbelievable.

12
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:38,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E03 -= Jealousy =- Subripped by zerox

13
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:42,140
可以了，谁要吃炒鸡蛋？
Here we go. How many for scrambled eggs?

14
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,900
好吧，谁要昨晚的牛肝？
Okay, how many for last nights liver?

15
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,680
谁要吃炒鸡蛋？
Now how many for scrambled eggs?

16
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:59,880
爸爸，我的科学实验遇到问题了
Dad, I'm having some trouble with my science project.

17
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,920
-要我帮忙吗？ -我想知道科学实验是什么
- You need some help with it? - I need to know what it is.

18
00:02:05,216 --> 00:02:09,792
-那么，你在研究些什么东西呢？ -科学知识呗
- Well, what are you studying in science? - Science stuff.

19
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:12,660
很好，这是个良好开端
Okay. That's a good start.

20
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,820
凯罗 你小学3年级时的科学实验是什么？
Carol, what did you do for your third-grade science project?

21
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:19,460
我制造了一种 单二氯化物和聚二氯化物的混合物
Well, I constructed a compound of monodichlorides and polydichlorides...

22
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:22,740
这种混合物可以承受极度高温和高压
that we're capable of withstanding excessive heat and mechanical stress.

23
00:02:26,537 --> 00:02:27,838
麦克呢？
Mike?

24
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,960
我测试超级球弹得有多高
I ran tests to see how high a Super Ball would bounce.

25
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,700
至少我们知道如何定义科学的界限了
Well, at least we've now defined the boundaries of science.

26
00:02:38,383 --> 00:02:39,980
-大家早啊 -妈妈早
- Morning, everybody. - Hi, Mom.

27
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:41,640
-你今天真漂亮 -谢谢
- Hi, you look nice. - Thanks.

28
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,340
的确是很漂亮
Wow. You sure do.

29
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:46,020
-吃炒鸡蛋吗？ -没时间了
- You want some eggs? - No time.

30
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,340
我8点半还有个 关于有毒废料的采访
I've got this 8:30 interview on this toxic waste story.

31
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:53,340
你知道吗？ 现在整个长岛都是这种有毒废料
Do you realize that they are just dumping this stuff all over Long Island?

32
00:02:53,398 --> 00:02:56,700
这些毒素很可能就在我们的水和食物里
It may very well be in our water, even our food.

33
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,020
甚至在鸡蛋里
Even in our eggs.

34
00:02:59,270 --> 00:03:02,307
我要迟到了，再见
I'm gonna be late. Bye, everybody.

35
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:05,279
-再见 -再见，午饭时候见
- Bye, hon. - Bye-bye. See you at lunch.

36
00:03:05,843 --> 00:03:07,246
午饭？
Lunch?

37
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,420
你说过回来一起吃午饭的
Yeah, you're gonna meet me back here for lunch.

38
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:14,520
简森，对不起，我完全忘了
Oh, Jason, I'm sorry. I completely forgot.

39
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:15,800
没关系
No problem.

40
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:17,580
那我们中午见了？
So, well see you about noon?

41
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,660
问题是我中午 也许抽不出时间回家
Well, the problem is I don't think I'll have time to come home.

42
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:24,240
爸爸，你的手艺太差 还是带她出去吃吧
It's your cooking, Dad. Take her out.

43
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:26,440
好主意
Good idea.

44
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:30,340
不如我到你报社去，和你到外面去吃吧
Look, why don't I just come by there and I'll take you out for lunch.

45
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,860
我不知道什么时候才有空
I'm not sure what time I'll be free.

46
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,620
简森，我不想你在那里干等着
Jason, I don't want you to have to wait around.

47
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:36,540
没关系，我倒很有兴致
That's no problem. It'll be fun for me.

48
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:38,380
我还没见过你上班时的样子呢
I haven't seen you in action at your office.

49
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:39,742
我…
Well, l....

50
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:42,240
你就答应吧，妈妈 他正求你和他约会呢
Mom, come on. The guys begging for a date.

51
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:44,415
他很少有这么主动的
I don't know how much more of this I can watch.

52
00:03:44,415 --> 00:03:46,818
-好，好.. -好吧，到时见
- Okay, okay, okay. - All right. See you there.

53
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:48,140
-再见 -再见
- See you later. - Bye-bye.

54
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,500
-再见 -太好了!
- Bye. - Yes!

55
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:59,360
格维克太太，水库里倾倒废物的事.
No, Mrs. Curwick, you see, we suspect that Easttown is giving you...

56
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,240
我们怀疑垃圾厂.
and your neighbors a lot of false information...

57
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,560
欺骗了你和你的邻居
about what's been dumped in that reservoir.

58
00:04:03,634 --> 00:04:04,935
对
Right.

59
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,720
我就是这个意思
See, that's just what I mean.

60
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:12,460
世上根本没有“含沙的”水
You see, there's no such thing as "chunky-style" water.

61
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:15,840
备案？好的
For the record? Good.

62
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,960
请稍等
Just one minute, okay?

63
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:21,240
周一如何？
How about Monday?

64
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:28,160
-可以打个电话吗？ -可以，在那边
- Mind if I make a call? - Sure, right over there.

65
00:04:33,865 --> 00:04:36,735
打电话而已，不是发射导弹啊
I wanna place a call, not launch an MX missile.

66
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:50,460
喂，我是西弗医生 请问安德森先生在吗？
Hello, this is Dr. Seaver. Mr. Anderson in, please?

67
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:55,440
不，我准是打错了.
No, I'm sorry, I must've misdialed then, I was....

68
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,920
不，我不是要登广告
No, I don't wish to place a classified ad.

69
00:04:59,357 --> 00:05:02,427
我知道价钱很公道
No, I'm sure that's a very good per-word price...

70
00:05:02,427 --> 00:05:06,628
我只是想打个外线电话而已
but no, I'm trying to get an outside line, here.

71
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,908
我没有要跟谁一起登广告
No, I'm not going to be placing the ad with anyone else.

72
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,440
我要找一个病人
I'm trying to reach a patient.

73
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:19,760
轻度精神分裂，偶尔的自大狂.
Mildly schizophrenic, delusions of grandeur, occasional....

74
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:22,940
就跟踪这件事，我们支持你
Let's go with this one. Yes, I'll be right with you, Mrs. Curwick.

75
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,460
还有这个
And this one.

76
00:05:25,516 --> 00:05:26,918
麦姬
Maggie.

77
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:36,100
刚才打到莫斯科了
I think I just leveled Moscow.

78
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:40,331
-我可以走了 -去哪里吃饭？
- Okay, I'm all set here. - So, where do you want to eat?

79
00:05:40,331 --> 00:05:43,373
-小麦，吃饭去 -小麦？
- Hey, Mags, wanna grab some lunch? - "Mags"?

80
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:46,260
弗瑞德，这是我丈夫杰森.西弗
Fred, I want you to meet my husband, Jason Seaver.

81
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,320
天哪!我竟然没看到你
Jeez, I didn't even see you down there.

82
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:53,200
杰森，这是弗瑞德
Jason, this is Fred Mathis.

83
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,100
我和他合作报导废料倾倒的事
Fred's the one I'm working with on the toxic waste story.

84
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:57,260
不必起来
No, don't get up.

85
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,960
-幸会 -幸会
- Hey, it's really nice to meet you. - Well, it's nice to meet you.

86
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:02,250
小麦经常说起你
Mags has told me a lot about you.

87
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:05,080
你怎么不告诉我弗瑞德的事？
Well, why didn't you tell me about Fred?

88
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,240
可怜的小麦整天对着我.
Well, poor Mags is stuck with me all day.

89
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,780
回到家当然不想提起我了
I'm sure the last thing she wants to do when she gets home is talk about me.

90
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:11,220
才不是
That's not true.

91
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,500
昨天不是说过吗？
I told you about Fred just yesterday.

92
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,140
不记得了？
Don't you remember?

93
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:16,933
是啊
Yeah.

94
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:20,360
因为你在我印象中.
I think I just pictured you differently.

95
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:23,777
是秃顶的，胖一点
Balder, fatter.

96
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:27,060
记者的公众形象就是这样
Well, that's the public for you. They think we all look like Lou Grant.

97
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:29,200
幸好小麦不是如此
Thank God Mags doesn't, huh, Jason?

98
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:33,060
我要和杰森去吃饭
Jason and I we're just about to grab a bite.

99
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,220
那不打扰了
Well, I wont keep you. Excuse me.

100
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:37,488
2点钟会议前.
Mags, I will need to see you for a couple of minutes...

101
00:06:37,488 --> 00:06:39,220
我要跟你谈谈
before that meeting at 2:00.

102
00:06:39,457 --> 00:06:41,166
现在已经1点半了
And it's 1 :30 now.

103
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:45,220
弗瑞德，一起吃饭吧
Well, look, Fred, why don't you just join us for lunch?

104
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:46,520
-我不想打扰你们 -我坚持
- I don't want to impose. - No, I insist.

105
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:49,360
-你们两个有公事 -杰森，你真的太好了
- You two have work to do together. - That's very nice of you, Jason.

106
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:53,340
垃圾厂的两个暴徒.
Mags, I didn't tell you, two of these goons tried to muscle me...

107
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:54,480
还想揍我呢
when I was out at that Easttown dump.

108
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:55,900
他们个子一定很高大
Must have been some big goons.

109
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,780
凯罗，为什么不帮我写论文？
Come on, Carol, why cant you just write this essay for me?

110
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,360
因为这是你的作业
Because it's your assignment.

111
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:04,160
你写得更好
Yeah, but you'd do a better job.

112
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:08,460
你若坚持下去，受伤害的是这篇论文
I mean, look, you're standing on principle and the result is that the essay suffers.

113
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,760
你没有良心责备？
Now, do you really want that on your conscience?

114
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,560
我宁受良心责备
That's the private hell I choose to live within.

115
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:17,091
麦姬
Maggie?

116
00:07:18,029 --> 00:07:19,829
好像是关车门的声音
I thought I heard a car door slam.

117
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:22,660
我也跟邻居说过好多遍.
No, you know, Dad, no matter how many times I ask the neighbors...

118
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,540
让他们从车窗爬下来
to please climb out through their windows...

119
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:26,160
但他们坚持开车门
they insist on using those doors.

120
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:29,580
麦克，多嘴!
Don't be a wise guy, Mike.

121
00:07:30,141 --> 00:07:33,614
-凯罗，表几点了？
-10：03 - Carol, what time does your watch say? - 10:03.

122
00:07:33,811 --> 00:07:37,581
-你的表坏了？ -没有，10：02
- Why? Is yours broken? - No, it says 10:02.

123
00:07:38,182 --> 00:07:39,982
还以为表停了
I just thought it might have stopped.

124
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,160
它显然停过，接着你上发条逼它再走
Apparently, it did, Dad. But it sounds like you've nipped it in the bud.

125
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:51,862
麦姬？弗瑞德
Maggie? Fred.

126
00:07:53,064 --> 00:07:56,070
没有，我会让她马上回电
Hi. Yeah, no, Ill have her call you right away.

127
00:07:57,500 --> 00:08:00,400
好吧，你也是
Okay. You, too.

128
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:02,660
再见
Yeah, bye.

129
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:05,977
弗瑞德？
Fred?

130
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:09,480
对，跟你妈妈一起报道有毒废料的人
Yeah, Fred's the guy your mother's working on that toxic waste story with.

131
00:08:09,814 --> 00:08:12,991
他看上去不错，很不错.
He seems like a nice guy. Very nice.

132
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:14,900
非常很不错
Darn nice.

133
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,640
你们别幼稚了好吗？
Will you guys act your age?

134
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:28,599
-大家好 -妈妈
- Hi, everybody. - Hey, Mom.

135
00:08:28,599 --> 00:08:31,834
麦姬，我没听见你关车门
Maggie! I didn't even hear your car door slam.

136
00:08:31,936 --> 00:08:35,011
下次我会用力点
Well, Ill try and do it louder next time.

137
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:38,920
今天大家怎样？做些什么了？
Well, guys, how's it going? What did you do today?

138
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:42,210
-我今天.. -小孩子没什么事做
- Well, I went-- - Nothing. They're children.

139
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,420
他们的生活枯燥乏味
They have boring, uneventful lives.

140
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:46,740
你呢？谈谈你的报道吧
How was your day? Tell us about that story.

141
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:50,800
杰森，真抱歉，午餐成了会议
Jason, I'm sorry our lunch got turned into a work session.

142
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,220
别逗了，我觉得还好
No, are you kidding? That was great for me.

143
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:57,200
我对淤泥的认识居然如此贫乏
It was shocking for me to discover how little I knew about sludge.

144
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:02,900
-垃圾厂怎样了？ -亲爱的，我累了
- What about the Easttown dump? - Honey, I am really bushed.

145
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:05,340
暂时不想提那些事
I'd rather not even think about that stuff for a while.

146
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:09,140
-可以吗？ -好吧
- Okay? - Okay. Sure.

147
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:11,560
爸爸，你忘了弗瑞德刚打过来
Hey, Dad, don't forget to tell her Fred just called.

148
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,880
弗瑞德？太好了，我正要跟他谈谈
Fred called? Oh, good. I need to talk to him.

149
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,340
明天得完成报道.
We're gonna break this story tomorrow...

150
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,500
即使今晚要通宵
if it means working till midnight.

151
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:18,760
恨不得马上揪住那群流氓
I just cant wait to nail those creeps.

152
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:21,740
弗瑞德，嗨
Fred? Hi.

153
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,640
开玩笑!
you're kidding.

154
00:09:36,834 --> 00:09:41,639
大家觉得我第一次烤的烙饼怎样？
So how did everyone enjoy my first foray into the wonderful world of pancakes?

155
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:45,640
已经超越煮牛肝的成就
Well, it beat the heck out of your foray into the wonderful world of liver.

156
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:51,900
爸爸，三年级时你做过什么科学课题
Dad, did they have science projects when you we're in third grade?

157
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:55,200
本，爸爸三年级时 连科学课都没有
Ben, when Dad was in the third grade, they didn't have science.

158
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,700
老实说，爸爸那时候 连三年级都没有
In fact, when Dad was in the third grade, they didn't have the third grade.

159
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:08,540
麦克，人说幽默感是儿童成长的最后阶段
Mike, they say the sense of humor is the final stage of child development.

160
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,360
你快要进入那个阶段了
You ought to feel it coming on any time now.

161
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:16,600
我三年级时做了个很好的课题
Yes, Ben. I did a wonderful project in third grade.

162
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:19,840
-我让面包发霉 -故意的？
- I grew mold on bread. - On purpose?

163
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:26,540
我认为霉菌在白面包上.
Yes, I determined that mold would grow faster on white bread...

164
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,340
比黑面包长得快
than on pumpernickel.

165
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,180
这样我应该换个方向了
I think I should strike out in new directions.

